// run
// `entryOf(f)` (§11.10) on the accepting path, so the IR differentials
// (`selfhost-diffir` / `selfhost-diffiropt`) cover the SELFHOST lowering of it,
// not just the checker's rejections in `check_entry_of_invalid`. Without a case
// that actually lowers, the seed and the self-hosted compiler could disagree
// about which symbol `func_addr` relocates against and nothing would notice.
//
// The assertions are the two properties that hold on every target regardless of
// how the image is loaded: one function's entry is invariant within a run, and
// two functions' entries differ. The absolute number is deliberately not printed
// — Mach-O output is position independent, so it slides between runs, while the
// static ELF output does not.
fn alpha(): int { return 42 }
fn beta(): int { return 7 }

fn main() {
  let a = entryOf(alpha)
  print("${a == entryOf(alpha)} ${a != entryOf(beta)}\n")
}
